#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The site's fonts move off Google: served from assets/webfonts/, copied from rnv-brand.
Built from: rnvizion.github.io@81f9626 · rnv-brand@db7dba0 (tree 7a7244a0) ·
Brand Infrastructure's note of 18 October 2026 · Chris's ruling of 18 October 2026.
Run from the site repo root, in a Codespace (it downloads 27 files from GitHub).

What it does, all or nothing (nothing is written until every check passes):
  1. Downloads the 27 files in rnv-brand's engine/fonts/ at db7dba0 (22 woff2 and
     5 OFL licenses) and checks each against the SHA-256 below.
  2. Writes them to assets/webfonts/, with fonts.css: the @font-face rules from
     rnv-brand's engine/brand.py --font-faces /assets/webfonts/ at that commit.
     Not assets/fonts/: that folder is gitignored and holds font.sh's TTFs.
  3. On every tracked page that loads Google Fonts, found by walking the repo,
     replaces the Google link with one link to /assets/webfonts/fonts.css and
     removes the two Google preconnects. Other preconnects stay.
  4. Changes the card generator's FONTS constant and its template the same way,
     so the next regeneration writes the same card pages this script writes.
Refuses if any page carries a Google Fonts line in a shape it does not know,
and checks that no Google Fonts reference is left in a page or the generator.
"""
